<section image-layout="blank" id="prO3YsZ8xH"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="z9_dnTRxVq"><h2>Recognition requires an independent other who can answer</h2><p font-size="18pt">The comparison isolates why acknowledgement loses value when the responder is denied equal standing.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="XKC923lmCG" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">One-sided recognition</p><h3>Dependence voids acknowledgement</h3><p font-size="16pt">If A denies B’s independence, B’s answer cannot carry the standing A seeks.</p><freeform-block w="390" h="112"><shape preset="ellipse" x="8" y="22" w="64" h="64" fill="surface" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="318" y="22" w="64" h="64" fill="surface" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3"></shape><box type="content" x="15" y="29" w="50" h="50" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed"><p font-size="18pt" align="center"><b>A</b></p></box><box type="content" x="325" y="29" w="50" h="50" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed"><p font-size="18pt" align="center"><b>B</b></p></box><box type="content" x="128" y="0" w="134"><p font-size="15pt" align="center"><b>acknowledges</b></p></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="84" y="32" w="222" h="14" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="84" y="68" w="176" h="12" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="270" y="61" w="2" h="28" stroke="accent" stroke-width="5"></shape><box type="content" x="96" y="88" w="166"><p font-size="15pt" align="center"><b>no equal answer</b></p></box><box type="content" x="301" y="88" w="98"><p font-size="14pt" align="center">dependent</p></box></freeform-block></grid-item><grid-item id="dxb3CApkve" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Reciprocal recognition</p><h3>Independence gives answers standing</h3><p font-size="16pt">Both remain independent; neither is reduced to a passive mirror for the other.</p><freeform-block w="390" h="112"><shape preset="ellipse" x="8" y="22" w="64" h="64" fill="surface" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="3"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="318" y="22" w="64" h="64" fill="surface" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="3"></shape><box type="content" x="15" y="29" w="50" h="50" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed"><p font-size="18pt" align="center"><b>A</b></p></box><box type="content" x="325" y="29" w="50" h="50" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed"><p font-size="18pt" align="center"><b>B</b></p></box><box type="content" x="100" y="0" w="190"><p font-size="15pt" align="center"><b>acknowledge · answer</b></p></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="84" y="32" w="222" h="14" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="84" y="68" w="222" h="14" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0" flip-h="true"></shape><box type="content" x="100" y="88" w="190"><p font-size="15pt" align="center"><b>listen · challenge</b></p></box><box type="content" x="0" y="88" w="96"><p font-size="14pt" align="center">independent</p></box><box type="content" x="294" y="88" w="96"><p font-size="14pt" align="center">independent</p></box></freeform-block></grid-item></grid><p font-size="18pt">In the seminar, permission matters when others can listen, answer, and challenge me in return.</p><p font-size="11pt">Source: <a href="https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/hegel/">Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Hegel”</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>